<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Only the keys Xcode's Info.plist generator cannot write.

	  The app target keeps GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE = YES, so everything that
	  can be a build setting still is one (Tools/generate-pbxproj.py,
	  APP_SETTINGS): bundle identity and versions, the display name, the
	  HealthKit, microphone, speech and calendar purpose strings, the scene
	  manifest and Live Activities. Xcode generates those and merges them on
	  top of this file at build time. It is the same arrangement Xcode itself
	  makes when a capability such as Background Modes is added to a target
	  that generates its plist.

	  The three keys below used to be INFOPLIST_KEY_* build settings as well.
	  The generator reads a fixed list of INFOPLIST_KEY_* names and drops any
	  other one without a warning, and none of these three is on that list:
	  every build shipped without them (the bundle dump in Screenshots run
	  36353047082 shows no background mode, no AlarmKit string and an empty
	  launch screen). Two checks now stand in the way of that happening again:
	  Tools/check-build-settings.py rejects any INFOPLIST_KEY_* name Xcode
	  would ignore, and Tools/app_bundle_contract.py inspects the Info.plist of
	  the app every workflow actually builds, and fails the run if one of these
	  keys, or a purpose string the app needs, is missing from it.

	  A key must be written in one place only: nothing below may also be set
	  as an INFOPLIST_KEY_* build setting (Tools/validate-pbxproj.py enforces
	  it), because the generated value would silently replace this one.
	-->

	<!--
	  Keeps Sleep Sounds, the Wind Down narration and Snore Check running when
	  the screen locks or someone switches apps. Without it iOS suspends the
	  process a few seconds after lock and the audio engine stops with it.
	  Audio only, and only while one of those is actually playing or
	  listening: Zoon declares no other background mode and never plays
	  silence to stay awake.
	-->
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>audio</string>
	</array>

	<!--
	  AlarmKit (iOS 26 and later) refuses to schedule anything when this is
	  missing or empty. It is asked for only when someone turns on the wake
	  alarm, asks Coach to set one, or starts a nap with an alarm (see
	  WakeAlarm and NapWake), never at launch.
	-->
	<key>NSAlarmKitUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Used only for alarms you ask for: the wake alarm at the end of your wake window, and the alarm at the end of a nap. Both ring even in Silent mode or a Sleep Focus. They are scheduled on this device; nothing about your sleep leaves the phone.</string>

	<!--
	  The system launch screen is a flat sheet of one colour shown while the
	  process starts, before any SwiftUI exists. Left at the default it is the
	  system background, pure black in Dark and pure white in Light, and
	  neither matches ZoonNightGround, so every cold launch flashed one ground
	  before painting another. LaunchBackground (Zoon/Assets.xcassets) is the
	  top stop of that gradient in both appearances, which makes the hand-off
	  into ZoonSplash seamless.
	-->
	<key>UILaunchScreen</key>
	<dict>
		<key>UIColorName</key>
		<string>LaunchBackground</string>
	</dict>
</dict>
</plist>
